# Lab 20: Fresh companion registration customer demo
#
# This REST Client walkthrough follows the successful notebook path:
#
#   Prep: acquire a delegated token and inspect inventory
#   Part 1: verify the existing Blueprint and Blueprint principal
#   Part 2: verify the Registry Sync Package and Agent Identity
#   Part 3: inspect an existing companion, or create one exactly once
#   Cleanup: optional and disabled by operator choice
#
# Run one request at a time. Never use "Send All".
#
# The normal customer demo is read-only:
#   Prep -> Part 1 -> Part 2 -> Part 3A -> Part 4
#
# Skip Part 3B because this experiment already has a companion registration.
# Use Part 3B only for a different, explicitly approved disposable source that
# has no existing or unresolved companion mapping.
#
# Required delegated Microsoft Graph permissions:
# - User.Read
# - CopilotPackages.Read.All
# - AgentIdentityBlueprint.Read.All
# - AgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All
# - AgentIdentity.Read.All
# - AgentRegistration.Read.All
# - AgentRegistration.ReadWrite.All (needed only for Part 3B and Cleanup)
#
# Put all real values in the shared ignored ../../.env file:
#
# A365_TENANT_ID=<directory-tenant-id>
# A365_CLIENT_ID=<public-client-application-id>
# A365_DEMO_TARGET_NAME=<selected-package-display-name>
# A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID=<registry-sync-package-id>
# A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-nested-source-agent-id>
# A365_DEMO_SOURCE_CREATED_AT=<exact-source-created-timestamp>
# A365_DEMO_SOURCE_MODIFIED_AT=<exact-source-modified-timestamp>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID=<blueprint-application-object-id>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID=<blueprint-app-id>
# A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID=<agent-identity-object-id>
# A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID=<successful-companion-registration-id>
#
# Preserve A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID exactly as Registry Sync returned
# it. Do not URL-decode and re-encode it.
#
# Save private responses only under:
# ../../evidence/demos/01-add-companion/
#
# The companion source ID used by any future Part 3B creation is:
#
# agent-governance:companion:v1:gcp:<exact-provider-source-agent-id>
#
# The companion already created by the earlier experiment uses the legacy
# committed-fleet:companion:v1 prefix. Preserve its exact mapped value. Do not
# delete or recreate it solely to rename the namespace.
#
# Never commit .env, token responses, raw responses, screenshots containing
# identifiers, or the durable mapping.

@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@targetName = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_TARGET_NAME}}
@originalPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID}}
@providerSourceAgentId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@sourceCreatedAt = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_SOURCE_CREATED_AT}}
@sourceModifiedAt = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_SOURCE_MODIFIED_AT}}
@blueprintObjectId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID}}
@blueprintAppId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID}}
@agentIdentityId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID}}
@companionRegistrationId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@readAccessToken = {{$aadV2Token scopes:https://graph.microsoft.com/User.Read,https://graph.microsoft.com/CopilotPackages.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentIdentityBlueprint.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentIdentity.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentRegistration.Read.All tenantId:{{tenantId}} clientId:{{clientId}}}}
@writeAccessToken = {{$aadV2Token new scopes:https://graph.microsoft.com/User.Read,https://graph.microsoft.com/CopilotPackages.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentIdentityBlueprint.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentIdentity.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentRegistration.Read.All,https://graph.microsoft.com/AgentRegistration.ReadWrite.All tenantId:{{tenantId}} clientId:{{clientId}}}}

###############################################################################
# Prep 1 - Confirm the signed-in operator
#
# Sending this first request triggers REST Client authentication. Version
# 0.25.1 opens the browser and copies a device code to the clipboard; it does
# not use the notebook's localhost authorization-code callback.
#
# REST Client caches the read token in memory for the other read requests.
# If a later request returns 401, clear the REST Client Azure AD token cache
# or restart VS Code, then send this request again.
#
# The optional POST and DELETE use a separate token expression and request
# AgentRegistration.ReadWrite.All only when one of those requests is sent.
#
# Expected: 200. Keep the returned user ID private.

# @name demoCurrentUser
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/me?$select=id
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Prep 2 - List Package inventory
#
# Expected: 200. Find the configured target only for visual confirmation.
# The remaining requests use the exact IDs from the ignored .env and do not
# match objects by display name.

# @name demoListPackages
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.1 - Read the existing Blueprint
#
# Expected: 200.
# Confirm:
# - id equals A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID
# - appId equals A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID

# @name demoGetBlueprint
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/applications/{{blueprintObjectId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprint
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.2 - Read the Blueprint principal by Blueprint appId
#
# Expected: 200.
# Confirm:
# - appId equals A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID
# - accountEnabled is not false
#
# The Blueprint object ID and Blueprint appId are different identifiers.

# @name demoGetBlueprintPrincipal
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintAppId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 2.1 - Read the original Registry Sync Package
#
# Expected: 200.
# Confirm:
# - id equals A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID
# - displayName equals A365_DEMO_TARGET_NAME
# - platform is GoogleVertexAI
# - the nested definition contains the exact provider source ID
# - the nested SourceIds identify a Connected Platform GCP record
# - agentIdentityId remains absent or null
#
# This Package ID is not the companion Registration ID.

# @name demoGetOriginalPackageBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 2.2 - Read the existing Agent Identity
#
# Expected: 200.
# Confirm:
# - id equals A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID
# - agentIdentityBlueprintId equals A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID
# - servicePrincipalType is ServiceIdentity

# @name demoGetAgentIdentity
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 3A - Read the already-created fresh companion
#
# This is the normal customer-demo path. It is read-only.
#
# Expected: 200.
# Confirm:
# - id equals A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID
# - sourceAgentId equals the exact value in the durable mapping
# - the existing experimental companion may retain the legacy
#   committed-fleet:companion:v1:gcp: prefix
# - everything after its versioned platform prefix equals the exact provider
#   source agent ID
# - originatingStore is GoogleVertexAI
# - createdBy and ownerIds include the approved operator
# - agentIdentityBlueprintId equals A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID
# - agentIdentityId equals A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID
# - managedByAppId is absent or empty

# @name demoGetExistingCompanion
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{companionRegistrationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# Part 3B - OPTIONAL one-time fresh companion creation
#
# DO NOT SEND THIS REQUEST during the normal customer demo.
#
# Send it only when all of the following are true:
# - the target is a different approved disposable source;
# - no companion mapping or unresolved earlier POST exists for that source;
# - the Blueprint and Agent Identity above were verified;
# - the operator has explicitly approved one creation attempt; and
# - A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID is empty because no companion exists.
#
# Expected success: 201 with a new Registration ID.
#
# On timeout, 5xx, or another unexpected response, stop. Do not send it again.
# On 201, immediately save the returned Registration ID in protected local
# state and set A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID before a later session.
#
# sourceAgentId deliberately differs from the Registry Sync source ID:
#
# agent-governance:companion:v1:gcp:{{providerSourceAgentId}}

# @name demoCreateFreshCompanion
POST {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations
Authorization: Bearer {{writeAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

{
  "displayName": "{{targetName}} - managed companion",
  "description": "Disposable independently managed companion registration",
  "createdBy": "{{demoCurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}",
  "ownerIds": [
    "{{demoCurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}"
  ],
  "sourceAgentId": "agent-governance:companion:v1:gcp:{{providerSourceAgentId}}",
  "originatingStore": "GoogleVertexAI",
  "sourceCreatedDateTime": "{{sourceCreatedAt}}",
  "sourceLastModifiedDateTime": "{{sourceModifiedAt}}",
  "agentIdentityBlueprintId": "{{blueprintAppId}}",
  "agentIdentityId": "{{agentIdentityId}}"
}

###

###############################################################################
# Part 3B.1 - Read a companion immediately after the optional POST
#
# Run only after Part 3B returned 201 in this REST Client session.
# It uses the ID from that named response and does not use the .env ID.

# @name demoGetNewCompanion
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{demoCreateFreshCompanion.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# Part 4 - Re-read the original Registry Sync Package
#
# Expected: 200.
# Compare with Part 2.1 and confirm the original Package identity field did not
# change. A successful companion does not enrich the Registry Sync Package.

# @name demoGetOriginalPackageAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Mapping checkpoint - no request
#
# Keep this relationship in protected state:
#
# platform                     = GoogleVertexAI
# providerSourceAgentId        = A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID
# packageId                    = A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID
# companionSourceAgentId       = exact saved mapping value
# current new-value format     = agent-governance:companion:v1:gcp:<provider-source>
# companionRegistrationId      = A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID
# blueprintId                  = A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID
# agentIdentityId              = A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID
#
# The deterministic companion source ID helps an operator understand the
# relationship, but it does not replace the durable Registration ID mapping.

###############################################################################
# Cleanup - OPTIONAL and irreversible
#
# Keep the following DELETE request unsent unless cleanup is explicitly
# approved and no dependent demonstration or experiment needs the companion.
# It deletes only A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID.

# @name demoDeleteExistingCompanion
DELETE {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{companionRegistrationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{writeAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# Cleanup verification
#
# Run only after the optional DELETE returned 204.
# Expected: 404.

# @name demoConfirmCompanionDeleted
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{companionRegistrationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0
